{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381207-gurahl-and-the-get-of-fenris","id":1381207,"title":"Gurahl and The Get of Fenris","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-13T21:47:23-07:00","id":1381207,"title":"Gurahl and The Get of Fenris","content":"This is a somewhat unusual question, but I'm going to try and explain it anyhow.<br /> <br /> One of my current PCs in a game, is the son of a Get of Fenris Elder Galliard and Jarl. His pack totem is Bear.<br /> <br /> Now I'm wondering according to the lore, what that would look like for a sept. More to the point, what kind of relationship, would a Get of Fenris Sept, led by followers of Bear, have with the local Gurahl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T21:51:49-07:00","id":1381209,"title":"","content":"Depends where the sept is, and if in America, where the Get of Fenris came from.<br /> <br /> In general, you lose the renown for Bear because of the Guralh. So if these Fenrir would be very ambivalent towards the bear pack and guralh. Of course, by myths, bears a very tied to nordic culture and I have headcanoned that Bear totem is more accepted among Finnish Fenrir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:08:25-07:00","id":1381212,"title":"","content":"Well, the Fenrir are of Swedish descent, and the sept is actually in Utqiagvik, Alaska.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T02:55:16-07:00","id":1381249,"title":"","content":"A lot of things affect the opinion on the Guralh, if the sept follows Bear then they are going to be more accepting of the Guralh. Especially if the local Wendigo have had positive relations with them and the Fenrir positive relations with the Wendigo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:56:53-07:00","id":1381301,"title":"","content":"A huge hurdle will be getting the local Gurahl to trust the Garou, children of Bear or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T07:24:16-07:00","id":1381313,"title":"","content":"In Alaska - a region I always wish had gotten a Rage Across book - it's probably not as big of a deal among the Garou establishment if a pack has Bear as a totem. It wouldn't surprise me to find Wendigo and/or Red Talon septs (who probably dominate northern Alaska) hiding the existence of known Gurahl from other Garou. Gurahl who come across the pack will likely find them at least worth watching, given that Bear has seemingly given them his/her approval, but will still be extremely cautious, spending a lot of time observing before deciding if its worth trying to making contact or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T14:57:42-07:00","id":1381769,"title":"","content":"The Honor hit for having Bear as a totem should be something that affects roleplay within the Garou. Bear is seen as inherently dishonorable because he and his children (Gurahl) won't share their secrets with the Garou and we're willing to kill Garou to keep them. So there is massive cultural prejudice against any Garou who associates with Bear.<br /> <br /> So while the Gurahl might be willing to talk with Garou packs who have the Bear totem, I think the greater issue of distrust is between other Garou and that pack. You seem to imply that being a member of a Bear pack does not actually do that in your chronicle because they're considered to be &quot;leaders&quot; of the sept. While it's possible for Garou in a pack with Bear to rise past these prejudices of the Garou Nation to become leaders in a sept, or even to a greater degree, I do think that should be something the chronicle should be addressing. There should be Garou prejudice against Bear packs, there should be resentment that such dishonorable Garou are becoming leaders in the sept, and there should be other Garou plotting against them as a result in order to preserve/save the Garou's honor or integrity. In other words, it is bad enough for a Garou to simply have Bear as his pack totem, but being friends with Gurahl - an old enemy - would be even worse.<br /> <br /> I understand this is not how many gaming groups RP it, but that is what I would do as ST.<br /> <br /> Going back to the Gurahl though, while membership in a Bear pack indicates these Garou might be trustworthy to begin relationships with, it is important to remember that there are mitigating circumstances. Garou do not always stay with a single pack. So what happens if you open yourself to that Garou, and that Garou subsequently goes to a different pack. What happens when those pack members are placed under severe social pressure by other Garou in their tribes or nearby septs to reveal any knowledge they learned from the Gurahl? What happens if a terrible event happens, and the local Garou use the Gurahl as a scapegoat to explain why it happened?<br /> <br /> So I think the Gurahl need to witness a lot more things for the Garou in this pack to do before they truly begin having positive relationships with them. Only as the pack members prove themselves will the Gurahl respond with more trust, more information, more favors, etc. The only thing membership in a Bear pack does do is open the possibility that such a relationship is possible, and to begin the process of establishing a relationship (and which might be ended, or stalled at any time based on pack member behavior).<br /> <br /> In terms of a member specifically being of the Get of Fenris, the tribe was known to be the biggest enemy of the Gurahl simply because 1) the Get were among the few tribes whose members could physically stand against a Gurahl, and 2) the Get are usually seen as the lackeys/muscle of the Silver Fangs. So it would be another sign that the pack member might not be really trustworthy and would need to do more in order to win the trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:27:55-07:00","id":1381778,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be more interesting if your group played as Gurahl instead : p","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:33:41-07:00","id":1381820,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> In this case, it's not a currently active part of the chronicle. Because the Elder, is actually my PC's father, not my PC himself. He serves in a pack under Mammoth, and is a Fostern nearly Adren.<br /> <br /> I asked, because I find it an interesting thing to ponder, and would like to get the input and perspective of others. In the current chronicle though, that pack are either Elders or Athros, and the pack Alpha is the Jarl or Alpha of a Fenrir sept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T22:35:07-07:00","id":1381861,"title":"","content":"I misunderstood. I thought it was your PC, not your PC's father. who was under Bear. In that case given that NPC's longevity, I think there's various ways to go about it. You just need to determine what the past history has been between the Gurahl and that NPC. It'll be on the past experience of several decades what their relationship was like.<br /> <br /> However, in terms of the sept, the other Garou packs may have their own ideas. Have they come around to support the leadership of the Bear pack? Or do they resent it? Have they decided to follow the sept leaderships' lead in their relations with the local Gurahl, or are they looking to turn against it? If they do support good relations with the Gurahl, are there any potential conflicts or misunderstandings? How is the sept's relations with other septs? Is there any pack at the sept that wants to be hostile and is preparing a challenge against the sept's current leadership?<br /> <br /> I think you can justify a lot of different reactions and status depending on individual personalities and past actions on both sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}